Description: Clipboard history for Cinnamon, MATE and Xfce
 Xclipy keeps what you copy and opens it, with an emoji picker, in an
 overlay under the text cursor when its keyboard shortcut is pressed.
 Its settings are in Cinnamon's System Settings, or in the settings of
 MATE and Xfce. In Cinnamon, a helper extension lets it work on Wayland
 too. With Satellite, copies from phones show where they came from, and
 items can be sent to a phone.
